# Git checks text files out with CRLF on Windows by default, and this repo
# compiles text into the binary: `include_str!` embeds skills/bytebase/SKILL.md
# and everything under vendor/bytebase/. Left alone, a Windows-built bbcli
# would ship different bytes than a Unix-built one, `install-skill` would see a
# copy written by the other as modified and refuse without --force, and
# vendor/ would stop being diffable against upstream.
#
# So normalise every text file to LF in the working tree on all platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf
